From: Time Machine ksmbd fix series
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ksmbd: fix AAPL copyfile COPYCHUNK with ChunkCount=0

macOS uses FSCTL_SRV_COPYCHUNK with ChunkCount=0 to perform an
atomic full-file copy when the server advertises AAPL COPYFILE in
server_caps.  Two bugs prevented this from working:

1. sizeof(struct copychunk_ioctl_req) == 33 due to the `Chunks[1]`
   sentinel member, but macOS sends exactly 32 bytes for a ChunkCount=0
   request (header only, no chunk descriptors).  The size guard
   in smb2_ioctl() rejected the request with STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER
   before it reached fsctl_copychunk().

   Fix: use offsetof(struct copychunk_ioctl_req, Chunks) == 32 as the
   minimum required size, which is the correct wire minimum for a
   COPYCHUNK request header without chunk descriptors.

2. The ChunkCount=0 path in fsctl_copychunk() did nothing but return
   success (the old "query limits" interpretation).  macOS treats
   ChunkCount=0 as "copy the entire source file atomically"; it does
   NOT send a follow-up COPYCHUNK with actual chunks after receiving
   the limits response.  The result was an empty destination file and
   Finder error -50 (paramErr).

   Fix: when ChunkCount=0 is received and AAPL COPYFILE has been
   negotiated, look up the source file from the ResumeKey, look up the
   destination from the IOCTL's FileId, and perform a full file copy
   via vfs_copy_file_range().  Report TotalBytesWritten in the response.

Tested: Finder Cmd+D duplication of HEIC, PDF, and plain-text files
all produce correct full copies after this fix.  Time Machine setup
and backup continue to work.

---
 fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c | 54 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 52 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
+++ b/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
@@ -7742,8 +7742,50 @@
 	chunks = (struct srv_copychunk *)&ci_req->Chunks[0];
 	chunk_count = le32_to_cpu(ci_req->ChunkCount);
-	if (chunk_count == 0)
-		goto out;
+	if (chunk_count == 0) {
+		/*
+		 * AAPL copyfile extension: ChunkCount=0 means copy the entire
+		 * source file to the destination atomically.  macOS uses this
+		 * when AAPL COPYFILE server capability is advertised.  Look up
+		 * the file handles, copy all bytes via vfs_copy_file_range, and
+		 * report TotalBytesWritten.  This is not the standard SMB2
+		 * "query limits" response (which also has ChunkCount=0 but is
+		 * handled before src/dst lookup).
+		 */
+		src_fp = ksmbd_lookup_foreign_fd(work,
+						 le64_to_cpu(ci_req->ResumeKey[0]));
+		dst_fp = ksmbd_lookup_fd_slow(work, volatile_id, persistent_id);
+		ret = -EINVAL;
+		if (!src_fp ||
+		    src_fp->persistent_id != le64_to_cpu(ci_req->ResumeKey[1])) {
+			rsp->hdr.Status = STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_NOT_FOUND;
+			goto out;
+		}
+		if (!dst_fp) {
+			rsp->hdr.Status = STATUS_FILE_CLOSED;
+			goto out;
+		}
+		{
+			loff_t src_size = i_size_read(file_inode(src_fp->filp));
+			loff_t copied = 0;
+
+			if (src_size > 0) {
+				copied = vfs_copy_file_range(src_fp->filp, 0,
+							     dst_fp->filp, 0,
+							     src_size, 0);
+				if (copied < 0) {
+					ret = copied;
+					rsp->hdr.Status = STATUS_UNEXPECTED_IO_ERROR;
+					goto out;
+				}
+			}
+			ci_rsp->ChunksWritten = 0;
+			ci_rsp->ChunkBytesWritten = 0;
+			ci_rsp->TotalBytesWritten = cpu_to_le32((u32)copied);
+		}
+		ret = 0;
+		goto out;
+	}
 	total_size_written = 0;

 	/* verify the SRV_COPYCHUNK_COPY packet */
@@ -8276,7 +8318,7 @@
 		}

-		if (in_buf_len < sizeof(struct copychunk_ioctl_req)) {
+		if (in_buf_len < offsetof(struct copychunk_ioctl_req, Chunks)) {
 			ret = -EINVAL;
 			goto out;
 		}
